# Host crontab for the two scheduled behaviours the behaviour spec requires (ADR-0007,
# spec §5 follow-up cadence, spec §10 audit-sample maintenance), run as
# `docker compose run --rm worker --job=<name>` — the same image and `--job` entrypoint the
# Container Apps Jobs design specified (ADR-0007: "Container Apps Jobs become cron"), so no
# application code differs between this deployment and the managed target state.
#
# Install (as the deploy user, from the repo checkout on the VM, e.g. /opt/erria):
#   crontab deploy/crontab
#
# Times are 5 minutes apart purely to avoid two `docker compose run` invocations racing the
# same Postgres connection pool on a single-vCPU-burst box at once — the behaviour spec does
# not mandate an exact time of day for either job, and both job bodies are stubs today (see
# apps/worker/src/jobs/run-job.ts), so there is no cadence-sensitive behaviour yet to tune
# this against. Revisit once #40/Plans 2-3 land the real job bodies.
SHELL=/bin/sh
0 6 * * * cd /opt/erria && docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.deploy.yaml run --rm worker --job=followup-cadence >> /var/log/erria/followup-cadence.log 2>&1
5 6 * * * cd /opt/erria && docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.deploy.yaml run --rm worker --job=audit-sample-maintenance >> /var/log/erria/audit-sample-maintenance.log 2>&1

# Monitoring (issue #61) — both scripts publish a custom Azure Monitor metric via the VM's own
# managed identity (deploy/scripts/lib-azure-metric.sh); infra/terraform/monitoring.tf alerts on
# them. Disk usage every 5 minutes: cheap to check, and the fastest-moving of the two — a log
# loop or a stray large file can fill 64 GiB in minutes, not days. TLS expiry once a day is
# plenty against a 90-day Let's Encrypt certificate; it needs DEPLOY_DOMAIN from .env, which the
# other two jobs above don't (docker compose reads .env itself; a plain script does not).
*/5 * * * * /opt/erria/deploy/scripts/report-disk-usage.sh >> /var/log/erria/disk-usage.log 2>&1
17 3 * * * . /opt/erria/.env && /opt/erria/deploy/scripts/report-tls-expiry.sh >> /var/log/erria/tls-expiry.log 2>&1
